  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU, TEI Green NEXUS Programme, 2024-2029 - ZAMBIA: EU, TEI Green NEXUS Programme, 2024-2029</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EU, TEI Gr&#xf6;nt NEXUS program, 2024-2029</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall objective (impact): To support a climate resilient transition towards green partnerships, sustainable growth and decent jobs in Zambia.

The overall objective is expected to be achieved by implementing projects and activities that directly contribute to the fulfillment of three identified outcome level specific objectives (1. to 3.) and expected outputs (1.1. to 3.1):

1. To enhance resilience of ecosystems and improve people&apos;s livelihoods based on landscape approaches along the agriculture-forestry-biodiversity-water and climate nexus.
1.1. Enhanced policy and capacity for integrated landscape management.
1.2. Enhanced capacities for watershed management, addressing forest degradation, biodiversity conservation, water resources management and climate resilience in selected target areas.
1.3. Improved capacity for forest policy, governance, management and monitoring systems.

2. To increase participation of smallholder farmers, particularly women and youth, in market integrated environmentally sustainable, resilient, low carbon, circular and nutrition sensitive value chains.
2.1. Improved delivery of transformative services to smallholder farmers, including women and youth.

3. To increase income opportunities and apply sustainable resource management practices for local communities.
3.1. Improved livelihoods through enhanced value chains development in forest products and services as well as diversified income generating activities within game management and protected areas.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta EU-initiativ syftar till att fr&#xe4;mja och investera i rehabilitering och h&#xe5;llbar tillv&#xe4;xt l&#xe4;ngs den zambiska delen av naturskyddsomr&#xe5;det Kavango-Zambezi genom att (i) &#xf6;ka ekosystemens motst&#xe5;ndskraft samt f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjningsm&#xf6;jligheterna genom integrerade landskapsmetoder inom nexus av jordbruk-skog-biologisk m&#xe5;ngfald-vatten-och klimat; (ii) &#xf6;ka deltagandet av sm&#xe5;brukare, inklusive kvinnor och ungdomar, i marknadsintegrerade milj&#xf6;m&#xe4;ssigt h&#xe5;llbara, motst&#xe5;ndskraftiga, l&#xe5;ga koldioxidutsl&#xe4;pp, cirkul&#xe4;ra och n&#xe4;ringsk&#xe4;nsliga v&#xe4;rdekedjor; (iii) &#xf6;ka inkomstm&#xf6;jligheterna genom till&#xe4;mpade h&#xe5;llbara resurshanteringsmetoder av lokala samh&#xe4;llen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This EU initiative intends to promote and invest in the green recovery and sustainable growth along the Zambian part of the Greater Kavango Zambezi trans-frontier conservation area by (i) enhancing resilience of ecosystems and improving livelihoods based on landscape approaches along the agriculture-forestry-biodiversity-water and climate nexus; (ii) increasing participation of smallholder farmers, incl. women and youth farmers, in market integrated environmentally sustainable, resilient, low carbon, circular and nutrition sensitive value chains; (iii) increasing income opportunities through applied sustainable resource management practices by local communities.</narrative>
  </description>
